    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">Compare two uppercase strings of equal length <var>a</var> and <var>b</var> character by character.<br>Output <const>=</const> if the two letters are the same.<br>Output <const>+</const> if the letter in <var>b</var> is the next letter of the alphabet after the letter in <var>a</var>.<br>Output <const>-</const> if the letter in <var>b</var> is the previous letter of the alphabet before the letter in <var>a</var>.<br>Output <const>?</const> if none of the above applies.<br>The alphabet loops in both directions:<br><br>Z &rarr; A<br>A &rarr; Z</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> An uppercase string <var>a</var><br><strong>Line 2:</strong> An uppercase string <var>b</var></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> A string with the same length as <var>a</var>, consisting only of <const>=</const>, <const>+</const>, <const>-</const>, and <const>?</const></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; length of <var>a</var> = length of <var>b</var> &le; 100<br><var>a</var> and <var>b</var> contain only uppercase English letters from A to Z.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">ABC\nABC\n</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">